<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Perdiccas II of Macedon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 413 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perdiccas">Perdiccas</a> II was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> from about 448 to about 413 BCE, who repeatedly changed sides between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a>. In 432 BCE he persuaded the Chalcidian towns to revolt from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delian-league">Delian League</a> and to concentrate their people at Olynthus, creating the core of the Chalcidian League.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/perdiccas-ii-of-macedon.jpg" alt="Perdiccas II of Macedon" width="320" height="158" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Perdikkas_II,_Tetrobol,_451-413_BC,_HGC_3-1-791.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
